WEBVTT

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.350
Cuticle Detective Inaba

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.620
Prime Minister

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.540
Do your best!

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.090
Secret

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.760
Meeting Room

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.480
Look! It's Inspector Ogino
and Detective Ogata.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:08.850
I heard they're pairing up.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.340
Even though everyone knows
they don't get along?

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.890
Seems they're going to
be in charge of the national

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.320
secret documents robbery case.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.980
I heard that they're
only pairing up for show

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.300
when they're actually assembling
two investigative teams

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.990
and pitting them against each other.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:24.410
They were going to take
advantage of their rivalry

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.950
and try to have this case wrapped
up as quickly as possible.

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:30.490
Judging by talent, I think Inspector
Ogino may have the upper hand.

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.920
I mean, he's got a cute
wife and Inaba Hiroshi.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.310
Hang on there, you mean
Detective Ogata.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:37.240
He's both light-hearted and light on his feet,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.120
and he's known to solve cases quickly.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.390
He loves dogs, and he used
to dote on Inaba Hiroshi.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:47.180
Guess it's ultimately going to depend
on who Inaba Hiroshi sides with.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.640
I'm not pairing with either of you!

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.080
Hiroshi!

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.560
Why the hell did you bring him, Ogi?

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.860
I didn't. He followed me.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:56.000
How dare you show him
the location of my agency?!

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.870
Your ears are as plump as ever.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:58.820
I'm going to eat them!

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.160
Sixteen hit combo!

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.920
Friend of yours?

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:03.870
Of course not.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.870
Defense Section Bodyguard, Ogata.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.960
I met him when I was in college.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:09.600
The departments we were in
were reversed then.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.710
Let go!

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:11.420
Nope!

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.040
When I transferred to the detective
unit, our positions switched.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:16.500
They must really<i> not get along...</i>

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.110
If only Ogino hadn't come along,

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:20.380
I would have ended up
being your partner, Hiroshi!

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.430
I said I'd partner with anyone
but you, and I got him!

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.220
He must have been really<i> annoying.</i>

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.680
Ogata is known to be
quite the dog lover,

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.210
Cause
of
Stress

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:28.290
Down with Ogata! Down with Ogata!

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.460
and police dogs that could no
longer handle his annoyance

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.390
would often go on strike.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.750
Ogata, that's enough.
It's obvious he doesn't like that.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:36.960
Where is that showing?

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:37.650
Now you're serious?

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:41.220
By the way, Assistant,
what are you trying to do?

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.280
Oh, sorry.
I'll peel him off immediately.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:44.910
He's rather shy,

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:47.280
and he gets like this when he
meets someone for the first time.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.110
I mean... how else am I
supposed to figure out

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:51.630
if they're friend or foe?

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:54.000
And am I a foe?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.440
Of course!

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.880
In that case,  how do you classify him?

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.460
His name is Ogata Yuzuki...

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:00.230
Foe.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:01.020
That was fast.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.840
Hey, Ogi, get him out of here already!

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:07.350
A masochist shouldn't be kicking
people like that, Hiroshi.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.810
I'm a sadist, you ass!

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.020
That's a lie.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:10.810
You're a masochist.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:11.800
A total masochist.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.250
Whoever you decide to pair with,
you will assist in this case.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.900
I don't want to pair with either of you!

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.520
What is this national top secret document?

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.360
I've never seen it myself, personally,

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:27.630
but it's a scroll that was
hidden in a forgotten temple...

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:28.370
Start

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.870
that had a board game on it.
Start

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:31.830
Is Japan really okay?
Start

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.730
Of course, it's not any
ordinary board game.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:37.060
I'll whisper it into your ear, Hiroshi.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.050
Don't you dare. And that's
not my ear; it's my hair.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:40.900
Start

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.720
As you can see from the replica,
nothing is written on it.
Start

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:44.120
As you can see from the replica,
nothing is written on it.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.020
However, when you throw the
die and take a turn,

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.410
words appear on the actual scroll.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:50.980
What appears is a date and an incident,

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.650
and the player can re-enact that incident.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.090
The goal is also left blank,
but those who are able to reach it

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:59.860
get the opportunity to
write in your future plans.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.080
For example, if I wrote:
"Hiroshi and I will live

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:03.710
together in a white house with a fireplace,"

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:04.750
it will actually happen.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.200
Sounds great.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.200
I'll stain the place red with your blood.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:10.200
Sounds super shady!

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:13.280
It had been passed down
with great care through

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.060
generations of prime ministers,
for use in national defense.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:18.210
But now it's in the
hands of some thief.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:20.540
There's no doubt this is the
work of a professional,

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.670
but we have no leads
as to who it may be.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:25.130
And
Japanese
history...
A shady scroll...
Professional
criminals...

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:28.610
The Valentino Family did it.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:29.640
You said it out loud!

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.350
What?! You've figured out who did it?

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:33.730
Aren't you two in a race, Ogi-san?

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.770
That was the perfect opportunity
for you to get ahead!

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.910
What? You're going to help me out?

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.210
Of course!

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:43.610
Thanks. Don't worry,
I'll win, no matter what.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.390
Huh? Something about
Ogi-san's head patting

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:47.970
makes me really happy.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:51.200
Maybe it's meant to create a
fatherly bond... I'm embarrassed,

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.300
but I didn't feel like stopping him...

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.090
Wow, you're looking rather
squirrelly, Inaba-san.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.120
We know where Valentino is hiding out.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.660
Let's go, Hiroshi!

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:03.300
Who cares about you?
I don't wanna hear it.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:05.250
Hiroshi?

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:08.010
What an annoying dog...

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:12.930
And now, we will be time traveling
through Japan's history, we will!

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.930
Have you forgotten our
main objective, Don?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.230
Worry not!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:22.190
I will finish this game and
become the king of Japan.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:24.820
Perhaps I'll isolate the country.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.300
Nothing less from you, Don!

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.530
Brilliantly acting like a dictator!

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.070
I wonder what I'll get from this roll?

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:32.030
We won't let you!

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:37.110
The police dog group:
The Cerberus Trio.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:39.960
I remember them!
So they're still in the business?

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.710
We did it, Hiroshi.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.670
We managed to get the
scroll before Ogino.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:44.900
You underestimate me.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:47.160
He's bagged a bag with a bag!

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.090
How can you have such
little regard for recycling?!

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:50.800
You're under arrest, Valentino!

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:52.550
Hey! I was first!

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:54.930
I will have Japan, I will!

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.890
Let's decide by playing the game.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.770
Sit

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.100
Not a single complaint?!
Sit

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:03.960
First, please get some
game pieces ready.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.520
When did you get the instructions?

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.730
Of course you last-minute participants
wouldn't have any ready!

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:13.070
Behold our magnificently
united game piece!

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:14.490
Why is it a marriage theme?!

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:17.850
Who knew a "Walking with Hiroshi" figure

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.680
would come in handy at a time like this?

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.620
There was no attempt to make
Inaba-san look human at all!

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.550
Look, Hiroshi. The media mix of love.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:27.350
Would that be classified
as flammable garbage?

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:30.340
Do we have anything we can
use as a game piece?
Oh, you don't have to be embarrassed.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:30.800
Ogi      Kei

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.170
Would these work?

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:33.800
They've already been used!

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.940
I will go first, I will!

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.850
Hey! Who said you cou—

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:40.060
CE57
King of Nakoku,
receives imperial
seal

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:42.540
What the hell?! Words actually appeared!

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.810
The imperial seal!
How fitting for m–

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.240
What... just happened?

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.450
They got sucked into the scroll?

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.370
It is the Kingdom of Na, it is!

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.030
Conditions for Return
Press the seal!!

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:00.170
Don, please take a look at this.

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:02.330
"Conditions for return:
Press the seal."

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:06.290
Meaning if we stamp the seal,
we can return, we can.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.690
Then, let us pay a visit to the ki–

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:12.300
Don!

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.510
Oh, hey. They're back.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:14.700
King of the
Japanese country
of Na of Han

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.000
That is not the proper way to use
the imperial seal, it is not!

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.100
Whoa! "King of the Japanese
country of Na of Han"!

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.220
I totally learned that in school!

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:23.790
Apparently, once a date comes up,
no one else can go to it.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:27.230
So as the game progresses,
you get closer to the present.

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:30.730
It'd be nice to avoid any
years with wars...

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:32.360
Maybe there are some rules...

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.070
Move carefully, you should.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:35.950
1600
The Battle
of Sekigahara

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:37.530
Go die!

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.120
Conditions for Return
Defeat six commanders
within four hours!!

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.140
Defeat that?

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.210
We're gonna die!

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:56.550
They're back! Kei, are you okay?

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:58.890
We didn't even need four hours...

00:08:58.890 --> 00:08:59.630
For what?!

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.150
1685
Edicts on Compassion
for Living Things
Proclamation

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:03.410
All right! Seems like
my kind of subject!

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.850
When did you throw the die?!

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:06.810
Conditions for Return
Pet all of the dogs!!

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:07.740
See?

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:09.520
Just shut up and pet them!

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:13.060
Hmm, this is strange.
This should be the last one.

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:14.280
Doesn't that hurt?

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.980
You can even bite me in the eye!

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:24.340
Welcome back, Inaba-san.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.050
Shut up!

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:25.750
What'd I do?!

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:26.090
The Burden Trio

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:30.030
Despite each team having a
burden, the game went on,

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:31.840
and we're finally near the end.
The Burden Trio

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.850
The goat team has been brainwashed by

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:37.830
Natsume Souseki and has forfeited.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:39.850
I am a cat, I am.

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.310
You're not doing very well yourself.

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:44.090
What are you talking about?

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:46.770
Sugita Genpaku just tried
to dissect me, that's all.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:48.980
Let's finish this, Ogi.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.450
I'm going to win.

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:52.440
I won't lose to anyone.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:56.150
Is it really okay to put off
arresting the goat?

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:57.650
Goal

00:09:57.650 --> 00:09:59.870
For us to win....
Goal

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.540
Ogi-san, we'll win if we
get more than a fi–

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.040
I was too late!

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:06.210
1918
Rice Riots
Occur

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:07.460
Conditions for Return
Eat the rice!!

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:10.670
It's a whole crop!

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.260
Bread ain't got nothin' on us!

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:16.600
I don't like these rice riots!

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:18.380
Such annoying rice.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:19.590
We're supposed to eat them?

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:23.060
There has to be a boss somewhere!

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:27.060
There's one that has been cooked.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:27.980
That's the boss!

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:30.800
What's wrong?

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:32.020
I want some salt.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:34.150
Let's eat it while it's still hot!

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:36.110
So full...

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.950
Is it okay to just leave these?

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:41.570
I'm scared to ask them
what they ate...

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:47.450
Not bad, Ogi. But as long as
I don't get a one, I win!

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:50.530
1972
Pandas
Come to
Japan

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:52.310
I, uh, like pandas, too...

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.000
Don't take losing so well, do you?

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.460
Bear!

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:56.510
Ogata!

00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:57.070
That's a polar bear!

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:58.540
Conditions for Return
Make it a panda!!

00:10:58.540 --> 00:10:59.640
Where's the panda?

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.220
Conditions for Return
Make it a panda!!

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.590
Damn, this is a little rough...

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:04.470
Move, Ogata.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.330
We're getting out of here.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:07.890
Hiroshi? What are you going to do?

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:09.800
This goes against my policies,

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:11.770
but I'll dye the bear's fur!

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.480
Bear!

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:14.440
Hiroshi!

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.880
Such moves!

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:21.160
He's a totally different
dog when it comes to hair.

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:22.360
Fast...

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:23.570
Orderly...

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:25.410
Minimal damage!

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.250
Is this what they mean
by "Cuticle Detective"?

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:30.460
All right. How does it look?

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:31.950
Bear!

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.170
Such luster!

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:36.810
Great job, Hiroshi!
You totally owned that!

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:37.760
It's nothin'.

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:42.510
We've lost the game, but let's
work together again, partner!

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:43.380
Wha–

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:44.680
Okay?

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:47.770
Get off me! This is the only
time I'm working with you!

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.270
My real partner is...

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:50.580
Just Ogi!

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.860
You two are gross!

00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:58.890
Ha. Loser.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:02.730
Well, it appears that I've lost
my partner and my assignment,

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:04.780
so I'll have to admit my defeat.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:07.280
He's so optimistic, despite his epic fail.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:10.450
You win. You can apprehend the goat.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.130
Right.

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.120
Valentino, I hereby...

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:16.890
Meow.

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:17.710
Cats?

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:19.290
Where'd the goat go?!

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:20.010
Did he escape?!

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.470
Come on, police of Japan!

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:25.610
You managed to retrieve the scroll,
but you failed to catch the goat.

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:26.640
Meaning...

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:28.540
It's a draw.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:29.600
How do you figure that?

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:31.960
Because it totally is!

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:31.970
Come on, let's go home.

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:33.450
Enough! Just help me find Valentino!

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:33.690
Okay.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:34.900
Anyways, Hiroshi...

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:35.980
Just shut up and find the goat!

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:37.950
Hiroshi, why won't you be my...

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:43.480
Botulinum toxin:
a powerful poison that can

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:45.580
kill millions with just one gram.

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:49.540
Said contents are waiting
for us in a safe, they are.

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:53.460
Our dealer didn't want
to meet in person,

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.250
so the key to the safe is
buried far beneath the earth.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.370
Sabako's grave
The marker is "Sabako's grave".

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.330
Sabako's grave

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:02.840
Only the best poison for the best Don.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:05.250
If we use it to produce
chemical weapons,

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:08.220
it will be very profitable, it will!

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.970
The area has been completely
excavated, it has!

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:13.100
Mother and Child

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.980
Meeting Room
Mother and Child
Stalker Case
Countermeasures
Headquarters

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:22.900
She won't even let a tree stand
in her way, will she?!

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:26.320
Egads! The key!

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.110
Mama!

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.230
Are you done playing in the dirt?

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:33.260
Then, let's return the nice dirt
to where it came from, okay?

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:37.500
You brat... How dare you
take my precious key?

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:39.710
I will take it back by force, I will!

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.310
Tink

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:42.710
Don!
Tink

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:46.620
Oh, no, Azusa-chan. It's not
nice to bury your friends.

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:49.940
Are you okay, Mr. Goat?

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:51.460
There, there.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:54.050
Do you hurt anywhere?

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.370
Nuh uh.

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:00.670
Good job, Mr. Goat. You didn't cry.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:02.940
Yeah! Mr. Goat is a big boy!

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:05.350
I'm sorry. You got all dirty.

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:06.860
I will go take a bath, I will.

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:10.040
Bye-bye, Mr. Goat.
Come play with us again.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:12.430
Bye-bye! That's a promise, it is!

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:16.430
Curses! The key!

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:20.020
I let myself be carried off
by the calming aura, I did!

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:21.840
Loren... zo?

00:14:22.530 --> 00:14:25.380
I shall be returning to my family home.

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:27.090
Farewell, Don!

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.400
It is a misunderstanding, it is!

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:30.020
Lorenzo!

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:33.810
If you're not in my life, I... I...

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:43.440
Inaba
Detective
Agency

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:46.040
Don't be so mean, Hiroshi.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:48.030
Get out of here. You're gross.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:48.860
Azusa-chan?

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.650
She's so cute!

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:51.440
Isn't she?

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:52.560
Want to hold her?

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:55.440
Gross. Look, I'm getting goose bumps.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:57.370
And I turned into an actual chicken.

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.490
Oh, my wife's here, too.

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:01.290
Wakaba.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:05.250
Hello, nice to meet you.
I'm Ogino Wakaba.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:08.310
Thank you for always taking
good care of my husband.

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:10.750
Your wife is gorgeous!

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:13.850
Nah, Azusa's even more beautiful.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.350
Wow. Doting daddy.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:17.450
Hiroshi, come here for a sec.

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.270
No. You're gross on your days off.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:21.850
It's about work.

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:24.310
Ogi-san is a completely
different person

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.000
when he's away from Azusa-chan.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:28.780
Stalker?

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:31.330
They're after Wakaba or Azusa.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:34.240
Well, I'm sure that'd be more
fun than stalking you.

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:38.400
I'd tell her to be careful, but she
doesn't have any sense of danger.

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:42.960
I'm surprised such a trusting creature
didn't get claimed by natural selection.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:47.100
So I'm asking you to be their
bodyguard for a while.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:49.420
What? The goat again?

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:50.650
Yeah.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.920
Apparently, he made a
huge purchase recently.

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:55.190
So we're tracking that.

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:56.830
Are you going to work?

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:57.310
Yeah.

00:15:58.030 --> 00:15:59.890
I'll come get you after work.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:01.670
I'll see you later, Azusa.

00:16:06.350 --> 00:16:07.320
See you later.

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:09.570
Don't be so embarrassed!

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:10.930
You want a kiss?

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.460
Octopus, I choose you!

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:13.320
Oh, my.

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:15.160
Yuuta-kun, that's too much!

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:15.930
Oh, hey! Stop!
Hiroshi.

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:16.740
Oh, hey! Stop!

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:19.950
If anything happens to Azusa...

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:22.780
I don't have to finish
my sentence, do I?

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:24.040
Yeah...

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.910
And so, while Papa Ogino is gone,

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:30.340
we will be guarding his wife and child.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:32.530
Failure in this mission
will result in death.

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:33.560
Yes, sir!

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:34.480
I can't hear you!

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:35.350
Yes, sir!

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:38.140
It'll be fine.
Kuniharu-san is a very kind person.

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.790
Ignore that idiot pacifist.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:40.770
Yes, sir!

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.350
Kei and I will watch over Azusa.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:45.780
Kei, if we're to die, we die together.

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:48.730
This isn't the first dangerous
bridge we've crossed.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.580
Yuuta, watch over Wakaba.

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:54.860
Listen up. This stalker's got some
guts to stalk Ogi's family.

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:57.570
Let's find him and take care of
business before they take care of us.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:58.810
Yeah!

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:01.950
The wolf and civilians are full of holes!

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:05.250
We'll grab our chance to
take the baby and the key!

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.040
The baby, as well?

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:11.450
If we take the baby,
the inspector will kill the wolf.

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:14.260
Nothing less from you, Don.
Truly underhanded.

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:17.220
Now, what are we gonna
do with the rug rat?

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:20.010
This might be the safest.

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:22.770
Inaba-san, let's talk about human rights.

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:25.810
And if you hold this one,
Kei, I'll feel even safer.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.980
What are you getting at?
I vehemently decline!

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:31.990
Sorry about the wait.
Play all you want.

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:38.060
Azusa-chan, stop! Wait, Azusa-chan!

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:43.120
It appears that, even in this day and age,
Japanese children like to fly kites.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.080
So charming.

00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:48.710
This just occurred to me...
Wouldn't putting a leash on her

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.440
make it easier for them to catch us?

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:51.420
Yeah.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.010
This plan is no good.

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:55.570
Azusa!

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:56.470
No! Come back!

00:17:58.490 --> 00:17:59.350
Ug! Ug!

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:01.930
Swimy! Swimy!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:02.930
Chirp! Chirp!

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.180
Hou! Hou!

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.230
Azusa, you need to stop...

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:07.810
Or else the circle of life will
get messed up here, too.

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.400
What's the deal with this park?!

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:12.220
At this rate, we're not going to last.

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:14.320
I guess we have no choice.

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:17.130
Look, Azusa-chan.

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:18.450
Let's play with blocks.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.240
Bwocks!

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:22.390
I heard before that she
likes to play with blocks.

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:23.540
We can finally relax.

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:37.490
It's done! She somehow made
an amazing log cabin!

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:40.720
Is this what the Ogino family
considers blocks?!

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:43.680
Let's think of something more girly.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:46.260
Azusa-chan.

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:47.970
Let's play house.

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.740
What part do you want
to play, Azusa-chan?

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:51.810
Papa!

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:53.770
Then, let's get this necktie on you.

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:56.520
Papa Azusa looks so cool!

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:59.880
Okay, I'll be the mommy.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:02.520
Do your best today at work, darling...

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.490
You all right, Mama Inaba?

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:16.260
Papa Azusa... already has
some skill at that age.

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:18.470
I saw a glimpse of a
whole new world...

00:19:21.650 --> 00:19:23.710
What were you thinking,
letting her go off on her own?!

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:25.550
Papa Azusa, come back!

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:28.680
Er... She's more efficient
than Papa Ogi!

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:31.070
What the hell?! Are you the
stalker, you stupid goat?!

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:34.110
Oh, hello again, Mr. Goat.

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:37.790
Did you come to play with Azusa again?

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:38.840
Thank you.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.570
No! It's a misunderstanding, it is!

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:43.930
That brat took my
precious key, she did!

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:46.390
I just wanted it back, I did!

00:19:46.390 --> 00:19:49.290
Oh, that's not good.
Let's give it back, Azusa-chan.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.200
That's a bad goat! He's Ogi's enemy.

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:55.960
I'm sure it's a key to some
safe that has botulinum!

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.320
We can't give it to him.

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:58.260
How sharp are you?!

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:00.670
So you're a bad Mr. Goat?

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:03.140
Well, you might say that, you might...

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:05.170
Make up your mind, bad goat!

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:06.600
Shut up, you wolf!

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:09.350
Stop calling me "goat"!

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:14.770
I am the ruthless villain,
Don Valentino!

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:17.690
Well said, Don!

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:19.480
Retreat!

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:20.030
Azusa!

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:21.440
H-Hold it! Please! If you don't...

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:23.490
If anything happens to Azusa,
you know what'll happen, right?
H-Hold it! Please! If you don't...

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:28.860
Lorenzo! Silence the infant!

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:29.770
Y-Yes, sir!

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:32.870
I have never seen such baby teeth!

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:35.880
All right! Wait right there, Azusa.

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:39.050
Mama!

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:41.300
Ma'am!

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:42.580
Once again, retreat!

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:44.220
Hold on, the key's right here.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.690
I-Is it okay to take it out?

00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:46.970
W-Will she be okay if I take it out?!

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:49.610
So this is the key that
Mr. Goat is looking for.

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:52.730
Oh, wow! She's tough!
Nothing less from Ogi-san's wife!

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:54.240
We have no other choice.

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:56.690
We will trade the key for the child.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:58.690
Everyone other than the
mother, stay back!

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:01.500
Or else you can say
goodbye to the little squirt!

00:21:04.010 --> 00:21:04.640
Bad!

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:07.940
I don't like mean Mr. Goats.

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:10.820
If you don't tell Azusa-chan
that you're sorry,

00:21:10.820 --> 00:21:12.750
I won't give you back your key.

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:19.880
I'm sorry, Azusa-chan.

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:25.220
Good boy. You were able
to say you're sorry.

00:21:26.140 --> 00:21:28.390
What the hell was that? Gross.

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:33.710
Lorenzo! I just did that
to get the key back...

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:37.640
The one at fault is this sow!

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:40.540
Calm down, you will, Lorenzo!

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:42.600
Be ruined, Japanese beauty!

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:44.400
Lorenzo!

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.590
Um... What about the key?

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:49.750
I think you may be able to destroy
the Valentino family, Ma'am.

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:51.580
I think they're collapsing
from the inside...

00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:54.170
Bye-bye!

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:27.660
Next Time:
"The Chocolate Enchantment Case"
"The Wolf Girl Assassination Case"

00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:30.180
How ya doin' lately?

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:33.310
Man, I've gotten more
gray hairs lately.

00:23:33.310 --> 00:23:36.060
Heard that'll get better
if you eat chocolate.

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:37.420
For real?!

00:23:37.420 --> 00:23:38.080
Nope.

00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:39.050
It was a lie?
